## Tests the role uses (need re-run / grub update when they fail)

1. Grub drift — intel_iommu=on must appear in `grubby --info=DEFAULT` args.
2. Grub drift — every discovered VF ID above must appear inside vfio-pci.ids= in those args.
3. Live — `grep -E '(^|[ ])intel_iommu=on([ ]|$)' /proc/cmdline` must succeed.
4. Live — if VF IDs were discovered: extract vfio-pci.ids= from /proc/cmdline and confirm each ID is present.

If hardware or VF enumeration changes, run this role again so vfio-pci.ids matches `lspci -nn`.

